# /sdd-prompts

Purpose:
  Automate prompt lifecycle: structure raw prompts, move to inbox,
  formalize, and archive after human approval.

Description:
  Scans prompts/ folder for unstructured files, applies structure,
  moves to inbox, then archives after review. Ensures all prompts
  follow the standard workflow.

Usage:
  /sdd-prompts
  /sdd-prompts --scan
  /sdd-prompts --structure
  /sdd-prompts --inbox
  /sdd-prompts --archive
  /sdd-prompts --approve <prompt-id>

Options:
  --scan      Scan prompts/ for unstructured files
  --structure Apply structure to unstructured prompts
  --inbox     Move structured prompts to inbox/
  --archive   Archive approved prompts
  --approve   Mark prompt as approved and archive

Behavior:
  1. Scan prompts/ root for unstructured files (non-markdown, missing frontmatter)
  2. Structure:
     - Add YAML frontmatter: id, type, status, created
     - Add Purpose, Description, Usage sections
     - Normalize naming: prompt-XXX.md
  3. Move to prompts/inbox/
  4. /sdd analyzes inbox prompts
  5. Human approves formalized prompt
  6. Move approved prompts to prompts/archive/

AutoMode:
  trigger: file created in prompts/
  scope: single file
  mode: background structure + inbox move
  approval: required before archive

Output:
  [scanned: X files]
  [structured: Y files]
  [moved_to_inbox: Z files]
  [archived: W files]

Rules:
  [PR-01] Unstructured prompts are auto-structured, never rejected.
  [PR-02] Structured prompts move to inbox/ automatically.
  [PR-03] Archive requires explicit human approval.
  [PR-04] Prompts are NEVER deleted, only archived.
  [PR-05] Duplicate detection runs before structuring.

State: +
